 13194139535239 true] [17592186339218 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339221 13194139535239 true] [17592186339218 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339222 13194139535239 true] [17592186339218 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339223 13194139535239 true] [17592186339218 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535239 true] [17592186339218 1041 "selection" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339218 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339220 13194139535239 true] [17592186339218 1110 #uuid "65bd660f-b589-5a19-b727-967684559e4b" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339219 1034 "$w$ only" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339219 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535239 true] [17592186339219 1111 #uuid "ba3c5034-e00e-53e8-b4fa-e87a1bcf2fc7" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339220 1034 "None" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339220 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535239 true] [17592186339220 1111 #uuid "6afb012e-f43b-5f26-b7e5-bcaddcd5f573" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339221 1034 "$u$ and $v$ only" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339221 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535239 true] [17592186339221 1111 #uuid "75e0b4e9-b4ba-5fa0-8c01-e169bc1d1c56" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339222 1034 "$u,$ $v,$ and $w$ only" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339222 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535239 true] [17592186339222 1111 #uuid "deed4926-2735-5948-a9f2-a013ce1428aa" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339223 1034 "$u$ and $w$ only" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339223 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535239 true] [17592186339223 1111 #uuid "bab50867-fb33-5144-a7b7-4401bc9c42cd" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339224 1017 #edb/ref 17592186339225 13194139535239 true] [17592186339224 1089 "q-135488" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339224 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535239 true] [17592186339224 1100 "Which of the following are stochastic matrices?\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}0.1 & 0 & 0.9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0.9 & 0 & 0.1\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}-0.1 & 0.2 \\\\ 1.1 & 0.8\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}0.5 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.5 & 0.7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339224 1113 #uuid "d9e8f97c-57bc-5f59-8108-1c5296ef33a7" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339224 1145 "Recall that a stochastic vector is a vector with nonnegative entries that add up to $1.$ A matrix is stochastic if all its columns are stochastic vectors.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices in turn.\n\n- Matrix $U$ is *not* a stochastic matrix since its second column is not a stochastic vector (the corresponding entries don't add up to one): \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0.1 & 0 & 0.9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0.9 & 0 & 0.1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Matrix $V$  is *not* a stochastic matrix since its first column is not a stochastic vector (it contains negative entries): \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-0.1 & 0.2 \\\\ 1.1 & 0.8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Matrix $W$ is a stochastic matrix. Indeed, each column is a stochastic vector (the corresponding entries are non-negative and add up to one): \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}0.5 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.5 & 0.7\\end{aligned}]\\,\\begin{aligned}0.5+0.5=1 \\\\ 0.3+0.7=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$W$ only.\"" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339226 13194139535239 true] [17592186339225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339227 13194139535239 true] [17592186339225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339228 13194139535239 true] [17592186339225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339229 13194139535239 true] [17592186339225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339230 13194139535239 true] [17592186339225 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535239 true] [17592186339225 1041 "selection" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339225 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339230 13194139535239 true] [17592186339225 1110 #uuid "40cfa081-d29b-57f7-a9f0-dc54a0338a6d" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339226 1034 "$U$ and $W$ only" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339226 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535239 true] [17592186339226 1111 #uuid "d8b4fbc5-a04c-5b22-b4cf-4bc2d56c5a72" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339227 1034 "$V$ and $W$ only" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339227 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535239 true] [17592186339227 1111 #uuid "11bb2216-6b97-5be8-98b3-b5f516c93f4f" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339228 1034 "$U$ only" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339228 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535239 true] [17592186339228 1111 #uuid "9162a11b-976e-5e4a-892d-9ce8f9899756" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339229 1034 "$U$ and $V$ only" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339229 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535239 true] [17592186339229 1111 #uuid "279a078b-cb83-5d69-89c6-4b12d0e6cdde" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339230 1034 "$W$ only" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339230 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535239 true] [17592186339230 1111 #uuid "786eb244-0f74-5bf7-93f7-0eb7dad83d5e" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339231 1017 #edb/ref 17592186339232 13194139535239 true] [17592186339231 1089 "q-135554" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339231 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535239 true] [17592186339231 1100 "There are two groups of children in a certain city: those who prefer ice cream and those who prefer cakes. A study has shown that, each week\n\n- from the children that prefer ice cream, $35%$ change to cakes, and\n\n- from the children that prefer cakes, $42%$ change to ice cream.\n\nWhich of the following tables describes how these children change their preferences each week?" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339231 1113 #uuid "1b2ff55d-f53a-5391-85d9-6aee7280619f" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339231 1145 "We are given the following situation for each week: \n\n- $35%$ of children who preferred ice creams swap to cakes. This implies that $65%$ of them continue to prefer ice creams.\n\n- $42%$ of children who preferred cakes swap to ice creams. This implies that $58%$ of them continue to prefer cakes.\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Ice-creams** | **Cakes** |\n| To: | **Ice-creams** | $0.65$ | $0.42$ |\n| **Cakes** | $0.35$ | $0.58$ |  |\n\nNote that we can write a corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0.65 & 0.42 \\\\ 0.35 & 0.58\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339233 13194139535239 true] [17592186339232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339234 13194139535239 true] [17592186339232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339235 13194139535239 true] [17592186339232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339236 13194139535239 true] [17592186339232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339237 13194139535239 true] [17592186339232 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535239 true] [17592186339232 1041 "selection" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339232 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339236 13194139535239 true] [17592186339232 1110 #uuid "da18d71e-b316-5416-b031-74a8bd55ec89" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339233 1034 "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Ice-creams** | **Cakes** |\n| To: | **Ice-creams** | $0.35$ | $0.42$ |\n| **Cakes** | $0.65$ | $0.58$ |  |" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339233 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535239 true] [17592186339233 1111 #uuid "940549cf-d44d-5a59-b03f-3ac2d3b64279" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339234 1034 "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Ice-creams** | **Cakes** |\n| To: | **Ice-creams** | $0.65$ | $0.58$ |\n| **Cakes** | $0.35$ | $0.42$ |  |" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339234 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535239 true] [17592186339234 1111 #uuid "591279c4-6bcf-5d4b-82b5-3275b1c2211f" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339235 1034 "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Ice-creams** | **Cakes** |\n| To: | **Ice-creams** | $0.42$ | $0.65$ |\n| **Cakes** | $0.58$ | $0.35$ |  |" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339235 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535239 true] [17592186339235 1111 #uuid "b66a82ad-b1b5-52bd-bf3f-503669a2e570" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339236 1034 "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Ice-creams** | **Cakes** |\n| To: | **Ice-creams** | $0.65$ | $0.42$ |\n| **Cakes** | $0.35$ | $0.58$ |  |" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339236 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535239 true] [17592186339236 1111 #uuid "20660e89-d1b1-516f-85b5-56d5c2571b50" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339237 1034 "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Ice-creams** | **Cakes** |\n| To: | **Ice-creams** | $0.42$ | $0.35$ |\n| **Cakes** | $0.58$ | $0.65$ |  |" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339237 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535239 true] [17592186339237 1111 #uuid "716fff59-4e43-5fa6-9c44-eb178499fff3" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339238 1017 #edb/ref 17592186339239 13194139535239 true] [17592186339238 1089 "q-135556" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339238 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535239 true] [17592186339238 1100 "A study shows that in a particular region\n\n- there is a $62%$ chance of another rainy day after a rainy day, and\n\n- there is a $55%$ chance of another dry day after a dry day.\n\nWhich of the following tables describes how the weather changes?" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339238 1113 #uuid "27fa3263-36e3-5305-83f8-d0188906560c" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339238 1145 "We are given the following situation for each day: \n\n- If it is rainy today, there is a $62%$ chance it will be rainy tomorrow. This implies that if it is rainy today, there is a $38%$ chance that it will be dry tomorrow.\n\n- If it is dry today, there is a $55%$ chance that it will be dry tomorrow. This implies that if it is dry today, there is a $45%$ chance that it will be rainy tomorrow\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rain** | **Dry** |\n| To: | **Rain** | $0.62$ | $0.45$ |\n| **Dry** | $0.38$ | $0.55$ |  |\n\nNote that we can write a corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0.62 & 0.45 \\\\ 0.38 & 0.55\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339240 13194139535239 true] [17592186339239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339241 13194139535239 true] [17592186339239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339242 13194139535239 true] [17592186339239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339243 13194139535239 true] [17592186339239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339244 13194139535239 true] [17592186339239 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535239 true] [17592186339239 1041 "selection" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339239 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339240 13194139535239 true] [17592186339239 1110 #uuid "a538507c-4c81-51a5-aafd-942ff5ef973c" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339240 1034 "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rain** | **Dry** |\n| To: | **Rain** | $0.62$ | $0.45$ |\n| **Dry** | $0.38$ | $0.55$ |  |" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339240 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535239 true] [17592186339240 1111 #uuid "e3c0b6e6-4b95-54fe-82a8-7d935bd53119" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339241 1034 "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rain** | **Dry** |\n| To: | **Rain** | $0.38$ | $0.45$ |\n| **Dry** | $0.62$ | $0.55$ |  |" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339241 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535239 true] [17592186339241 1111 #uuid "213007d7-02a0-5480-a695-99e3de3a68cf" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339242 1034 "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rain** | **Dry** |\n| To: | **Rain** | $0.45$ | $0.38$ |\n| **Dry** | $0.55$ | $0.62$ |  |" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339242 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535239 true] [17592186339242 1111 #uuid "b3ab16f2-8651-5f58-b192-80bc6e0ee97b" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339243 1034 "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rain** | **Dry** |\n| To: | **Rain** | $0.62$ | $0.55$ |\n| **Dry** | $0.38$ | $0.45$ |  |" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339243 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535239 true] [17592186339243 1111 #uuid "a7902499-2284-5831-a9a7-7969589eb875" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339244 1034 "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rain** | **Dry** |\n| To: | **Rain** | $0.45$ | $0.62$ |\n| **Dry** | $0.55$ | $0.38$ |  |" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339244 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535239 true] [17592186339244 1111 #uuid "25f39168-7656-5388-986f-ec3e14112dd5" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339245 1017 #edb/ref 17592186339246 13194139535239 true] [17592186339245 1089 "q-135565" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339245 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535239 true] [17592186339245 1100 "A study shows that for a particular area in a specific season,\n\n- on a day that follows a day without precipitation, there is a $25%$ chance to have rain and a $35%$ chance to have snow.\n\n- on a day that follows a rainy day, there is a $40%$ chance not to have precipitation and a $5%$ chance to have snow.\n\n- on a day that follows a snowy day, there is a $50%$ chance not to have precipitation and a $5%$ chance to have rain.\n\nThe stochastic matrix that describes this situation is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}a & 0.4 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.25 & b & 0.05 \\\\ 0.35 & 0.05 & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339245 1113 #uuid "1e83e16e-b8fd-55a5-9aa6-130410640d20" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339245 1145 "We are given the following situation for this area:\n\n- On a day that follows a day without precipitation, there is a $25%$ chance to have rain and a $35%$ chance to have snow. This implies a $40%$ chance of not having precipitation on this day.\n\n- On a day that follows a rainy day, there is a $40%$ chance not to have precipitation and a $5%$ chance to have snow. This implies a $55%$ chance of having rain on this day.\n\n- On a day that follows a snowy day, there is a $50%$ chance not to have precipitation and a $5%$ chance to have rain. This implies a $45%$ chance of having snow on this day.\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **No Precipitation** | **Rain** | **Snow** |\n| To: | **No Precipitation** | $0.4$ | $0.4$ | $0.5$ |\n| **Rain** | $0.25$ | $0.55$ | $0.05$ |  |\n| **Snow** | $0.35$ | $0.05$ | $0.45$ |  |\n\nWe can write the corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 & 0.4 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.25 & 0.55 & 0.05 \\\\ 0.35 & 0.05 & 0.45\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0.4+0.55+0.45=1.4.\n$$" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339247 13194139535239 true] [17592186339246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339248 13194139535239 true] [17592186339246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339249 13194139535239 true] [17592186339246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339250 13194139535239 true] [17592186339246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339251 13194139535239 true] [17592186339246 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535239 true] [17592186339246 1041 "selection" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339246 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339248 13194139535239 true] [17592186339246 1110 #uuid "794c005a-3524-518c-807a-62738cd42c88" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339247 1034 "0.6" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339247 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535239 true] [17592186339247 1111 #uuid "f0e1c674-7298-5cf6-b1c4-7864248e31b0" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339248 1034 "1.4" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339248 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535239 true] [17592186339248 1111 #uuid "ee7cb24b-3fa3-5d91-8915-efbde55bcc63" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339249 1034 "0.8" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339249 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535239 true] [17592186339249 1111 #uuid "ee00f827-07ae-5f2b-989e-c07f5addf3d7" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339250 1034 "0.75" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339250 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535239 true] [17592186339250 1111 #uuid "78376574-492b-5e5f-a57f-809c997a9bd4" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339251 1034 "0.95" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339251 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535239 true] [17592186339251 1111 #uuid "9fd55427-5528-5be3-893e-c5c17cfcb5b7" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339252 1017 #edb/ref 17592186339253 13194139535239 true] [17592186339252 1089 "q-135566" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339252 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535239 true] [17592186339252 1100 "There are three cable TV providers in a particular apartment block: provider $A,$ provider $B,$ and provider $C.$ A study has shown that, each year\n\n- from the tenants using provider $A,$ $80%$ swap to provider $B$ and $10%$ swap to provider $C,$\n\n- from the tenants using provider $B,$ $25%$ swap to provider $A$ and $25%$ swap to provider $C,$\n\n- from the tenants using provider $C,$ $70%$ swap to provider $A$ and $10%$ swap to provider $B.$\n\nThe stochastic matrix that describes this situation is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.1 & a & 0.7 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.5 & b \\\\ c & 0.25 & 0.2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339252 1113 #uuid "e269fcad-8675-50e2-b907-1b09ce78f588" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339252 1145 "We are given the following situation for each year:\n\n- From the tenants using provider $A,$ $80%$ swap to provider $B$ and $10%$ swap to provider $C.$  This implies that $10%$ of them continue using provider $A.$\n\n- From the tenants using provider $B,$ $25%$ swap to provider $A$ and $25%$ swap to provider $C.$ This implies that $50%$ of them continue using provider $B.$\n\n- From the tenants using provider $C,$ $70%$ swap to provider $A$ and $10%$ swap to provider $B.$ This implies that $20%$ of them continue using provider $C.$\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Provider A** | **Provider B** | **Provider C** |\n| To: | **Provider A** | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.7$ |\n| **Provider B** | $0.8$ | $0.5$ | $0.1$ |  |\n| **Provider C** | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ |  |\n\nWe can write the corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.1 & 0.25 & 0.7 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.5 & 0.1 \\\\ 0.1 & 0.25 & 0.2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0.25+0.1+0.1=0.45.\n$$" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339253 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339254 13194139535239 true] [17592186339253 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339255 13194139535239 true] [17592186339253 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339256 13194139535239 true] [17592186339253 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339257 13194139535239 true] [17592186339253 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339258 13194139535239 true] [17592186339253 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535239 true] [17592186339253 1041 "selection" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339253 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339257 13194139535239 true] [17592186339253 1110 #uuid "70dae69e-1f08-56a4-9010-50d401036fd0" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339254 1034 "0.7" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339254 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535239 true] [17592186339254 1111 #uuid "f7bf1303-5570-5700-9fd6-556fc2eef36a" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339255 1034 "1.25" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339255 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535239 true] [17592186339255 1111 #uuid "3bc0e126-c04b-54a2-8ff4-bacf99c7f908" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339256 1034 "1" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339256 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535239 true] [17592186339256 1111 #uuid "cc5160a5-9c20-5ada-89be-2916efdec933" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339257 1034 "0.45" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339257 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535239 true] [17592186339257 1111 #uuid "f204d38d-30bf-589a-be26-2341da76de50" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339258 1034 "0.55" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339258 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535239 true] [17592186339258 1111 #uuid "2dd3e102-bfe1-5ed3-9404-9d359d8d8ee5" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339259 1017 #edb/ref 17592186339260 13194139535239 true] [17592186339259 1089 "q-35789" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339259 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535239 true] [17592186339259 1100 "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.25 & 0.85 \\\\ 0.75 & 0.15\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 \\\\ 0.6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \nConsider a Markov chain with the stochastic matrix $P$ and the initial state vector ${x}_{0}$ given above. Calculate the state vector ${x}_{2}.$" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339259 1113 #uuid "b15112f4-7893-524a-8de9-46c29499aff4" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339259 1145 "To find the state vector ${x}_{2},$ we apply two steps of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0},\\,{x}_{2}=P{x}_{1}\n$$\n\nAfter the first step, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.25 & 0.85 \\\\ 0.75 & 0.15\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0.4 \\\\ 0.6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.61 \\\\ 0.39\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, after the second step, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =P{x}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.25 & 0.85 \\\\ 0.75 & 0.15\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0.61 \\\\ 0.39\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.484 \\\\ 0.516\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339261 13194139535239 true] [17592186339260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339262 13194139535239 true] [17592186339260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339263 13194139535239 true] [17592186339260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339264 13194139535239 true] [17592186339260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339265 13194139535239 true] [17592186339260 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535239 true] [17592186339260 1041 "selection" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339260 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339264 13194139535239 true] [17592186339260 1110 #uuid "f18b001c-3561-5a01-ad1b-840a72b9f3e3" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339261 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}0.61 \\\\ 0.39\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535239 true] [17592186339261 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535239 true] [17592186339261 1111 #uuid "be445be2-e50f-5cae-92ce-28fb012212d4" 13194139535239 true] [